If you're deploying an application from scratch — what all do you need?

Interviewer:
Imagine you have a codebase. From scratch — what all would you set up to take it live in production?



Sure! Here's a step-by-step breakdown of everything needed — from code to production:
1. Source Code Management
Store the code in a Git repository (e.g., GitHub, Azure Repos, GitLab)
Use proper branching strategy (main, dev, feature/*)
So that multiple people can collaborate and track changes.

2.Build Process
Define how the application will be built (Node, Python, Java etc.)
Install dependencies, run tests, create artifacts
This ensures the code compiles and works before shipping.

3. Containerization (Optional but recommended)
Use Docker to package the app with its dependencies
Write a Dockerfile
Build and push image to container registry (ACR, DockerHub etc.)
“Works on my machine” ends here.

4. Infrastructure Setup
Set up infrastructure to run the app (VMs, AKS, ECS, etc.)
Use Terraform, ARM, Bicep, CloudFormation (IaC)
Manual infra setup is risky and inconsistent.

5. Networking & DNS
Setup Load Balancers, Ingress, DNS records (like app.justvisualise.com)
So users can access the app from anywhere.

6. Secrets & Config Management
Environment variables, secrets (DB creds, API keys) via Key Vault, Sealed Secrets, etc.
Never hardcode secrets in code.

7. CI/CD Pipeline
Create pipeline to:
Build app
Run tests
Build Docker image
Push to registry
Deploy to Dev/UAT/Prod
Tools: Azure Pipelines, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, GitLab CI etc.

8. Monitoring & Logging
Set up tools to monitor app & infra (Grafana, Prometheus, Azure Monitor)
Central logging (ELK, Loki, Azure Log Analytics)
Helps in debugging and performance tuning.

9. Testing & Staging Environment
Deploy to Dev & UAT before Prod
Run automated and manual tests
Catch issues before real users do.

10. Rollback Plan
Use Helm or Kubernetes Deployment strategies
Keep previous builds ready for rollback
Deployment without rollback = risky launch.



Ek app ko live karne ka matlab sirf code run karna nahi hai.
 Aapko infra banana hota hai, pipeline lagani hoti hai, secrets secure karne hote hain, aur monitoring bhi lagani hoti hai.
Agar aap ye poori chain samajh jaate ho — toh aap DevOps ki asli value samajhne lagte ho.


Interview Wrap-Up Answer:
To deploy an application from scratch, we need source code management, build automation, containerization, infrastructure setup, networking, secrets/config management, CI/CD pipeline, monitoring, and testing stages. All this ensures reliable, repeatable, and secure deployment to production.
